    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cursorword\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently to overwrite the default highlighting groups you need to do so manually\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.cursorword').setup({ })\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniCursorWord', { link = 'Visual' })\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniCursorWordCurrent', { link = 'CursorLine' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich is totally fine. However, this does not handle the case when the user switches the color scheme. So you need to add another helper\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.cursorword').setup({})\r\nlocal function set_mini_highlights()\r\n    vim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniCursorWord', { link = 'Visual' })\r\n    vim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniCursorWordCurrent', { link = 'CursorLine' })\r\nend\r\nset_mini_highlights() -- call initially to override default style\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ColorScheme', { callback = set_mini_highlights }) -- call when a colour scheme changes\r\n```\r\n\r\nSince this plugin already handles the recreation of highlighting groups on colour scheme changes, would it be possible to provide a custom highlighting group definition as part of the options?\r\n\r\nHere is an example of what this might look like, there is probably a better naming convention but this conveys the idea.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.cursorword').setup({\r\n    hi_cursorword = { link = 'Visual' }, -- vim.api.keyset.highlight\r\n    hi_cursorword_current = { link = 'CursorLine' },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nPS:  Thank you for your work!\r\n",
