        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nRelying on built-in mechanism of highlight group is one of the core [general principles](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim?tab=readme-ov-file#general-principles) of 'mini.nvim' (see \"Highlighting\" section). This approach allows (more or less) delegating highlight group management to a known and extensively documented built-in methods.\r\n\r\n> Since this plugin already handles the recreation of highlighting groups on colour scheme changes, would it be possible to provide a custom highlighting group definition as part of the options?\r\n\r\nThis is done only because there is no way to create persistent default highlight group which is not a link. That said, maybe it is reasonable to change them to link to `Underlined` group by default...\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
